    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "Active downstream gate after #245 `FULL_CHARACTER_MODEL_LOCK_R02 = PASS`.\n\nPurpose: prove how the already-defined ZORR ivory suit deforms under a small set of real pose forces without redesigning the character or turning the sheet into realism study.\n\nAuthority inputs:\n- accepted suit turnaround;\n- accepted costume/accessory sheet;\n- `BODY_CONSTRUCTION_R01`;\n- `HANDS_CANON_R03` / `HAND_EXPRESSION_R01` for cuff/watch interaction;\n- current ZORR fold law: folds only where force requires; ivory remains calm; 2–5 meaningful fold shapes per large garment region.\n\nTarget high-information controls:\n1. shoulder/arm raise — shoulder seam + armpit tension;\n2. elbow bend — sleeve compression + cuff/watch;\n3. torso twist — lapel/chest/waist relationship;\n4. seated hip/waist compression — jacket hem + trouser waist/crotch;\n5. knee bend — trouser knee compression/tension;\n6. stride/ankle — trouser break + shoe relation.\n\nHard law: anime readability and large graphic garment planes outrank realistic cloth simulation. No decorative wrinkle noise.\n\nNo image generation/editing is authorized by this tracker. Visual execution requires separate OWNER authorization under current image rule.\n\nTerminal goal: `COSTUME_MECHANICS_R01 = PASS` when attachment anchors stay invariant, force-driven folds are repeatable, silhouette remains fashion-first, and no hidden costume redesign appears.",
